 out=R/'verify/out/n100-uniform-outer-ear-topology.json';need(not out.exists(),'overwrite');out.write_text(json.dumps({'schema':'n100-uniform-outer-ear-topology/v1','radius_upper':str(rho),'rows':rows,'analytic_proof_steps':['for 0<r<=rho and theta<=2asin(r), H_r(theta)<=H_rho(theta), because only sin(theta/2)*sqrt(r^2-sin^2(theta/2)) depends on r and is increasing','ear three-arc sum S<=2asin(2r)<=2asin(2rho)<gamma; all individual arcs remain in H_rho domain','Jensen at fixed rho bounds sums by F(S)=3H_rho(S/3)+(B-3)H_rho((2pi-S)/(B-3))','on its feasible argument interval, F is increasing for S<=6pi/B by concavity of H_rho; gamma<6pi/B, and both gamma-group arguments lie in H_rho domain','replace S by gamma, replace triangle factor C*r^2 by C*rho^2 with C>0, then use both saved positive endpoint gaps','no ear means no face has2boundary edges; a3boundary-edge triangle would constitute whole triangulated disk and is impossible since m>B>3','every boundary edge incident to1triangle; with each triangle having<=1boundary edge, exactly B distinct one-boundary-edge faces; Euler total2m-B-2'], 'scope':'uniform ear prohibition for same-radius normalized diagrams with specified m,B at any0<r<=rho; topology may change with r, proof applies afresh to each diagram; analytic H concavity and common-diagram geometry inherited, not formalized','global_optimality':False,'bindings':{str(q.relative_to(R)):hashlib.sha256(q.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for q in [p,ip]},'script_sha256':hashlib.sha256(Path(__file__).read_bytes()).hexdigest()},indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8');print('PASS uniform outer ear and face counts',[(c['m'],c['B'],c['faces_with_zero_boundary_edges'],c['faces_with_one_boundary_edge']) for c in rows])
